# project_index.md

## Purpose

This file defines how Revtek vehicle projects should be organized and referenced.

Revtek works with complete vehicle customization projects in addition to individual product sales.

A project may combine multiple products, sourcing activities, installation work, fitment, finishing, and final delivery.

## Project Structure

Each project should ideally contain:

* Project ID
* Project name
* Customer ID
* Vehicle
* Vehicle model
* Vehicle generation
* Vehicle year
* Project status
* Project objective
* Selected products
* Product IDs
* Supplier information
* Order information
* Installation requirements
* Installation status
* Project timeline
* Project costs
* Customer price
* Project images
* Before images
* During-project images
* Final images
* Notes

## Project Status

Recommended project stages:

1. Lead
2. Consultation
3. Project Planning
4. Quotation
5. Customer Confirmation
6. Product Ordering
7. Product In Transit
8. Product Received
9. Installation Scheduled
10. Installation
11. Fitment / QC
12. Completed
13. Delivered
14. After-sales

## Project Principle

A project should be understood as the complete customer outcome rather than simply a collection of products.

## AI Rules

When discussing a project:

* Use the Project ID as the primary reference.
* Do not assume project completion.
* Do not assume installation has happened.
* Do not assume a customer has approved a quotation.
* Do not publish private customer information.
* Do not use unfinished project information as a completed case study.
* Use project records as the source of truth.

